# The build context for `deploy/demo/app.Dockerfile`, whose context is this
# directory (`demo-infrastructure` 2.1). What the image needs is the source the
# two workspaces build from; everything else is either rebuilt inside the image,
# irrelevant to it, or actively wrong in it.
#
# The index image does not read this file: its context is `deploy/demo/` and
# `mini-classify` reaches it as a named build context (see index.Dockerfile).

# Installed inside the image, from the lockfile. Also the single largest thing
# in this tree, and copying a host `node_modules` in would put this machine's
# platform binaries in a Linux image.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Built inside the image by stage one. A stale local `dist` copied in would be
# served instead of the build that was just made.
client/dist

.git
.gitignore

# The deployment's own files. `config.json` is mounted from the checkout at
# runtime and must exist in exactly one place with one age (D6), so it must not
# also be a layer; the Dockerfiles and the Caddyfiles are read by the builder
# and by Caddy, never by the app.
deploy

# Prose, specifications and tooling: none of it is imported by the source.
openspec
docs
scripts
README.md
CLAUDE.md
.node-version

.playwright-mcp
.claude
*.log
